  "goodToKnow": "Die Kläranlage is a sewage treatment plant that cleans Abwasser (waste water) mechanically, biologically and chemically. Germany has around 9,000 of them. Since the pandemic, many plants are monitored for viruses (Abwassermonitoring) to detect outbreaks early. Der Klärschlamm (sewage sludge) is increasingly burned rather than spread on fields. Klären also means to clarify: eine Frage klären. Plural: die Kläranlagen."
